<title>ITALY: SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ITALIAN FIRST DIVISION SCORERS.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Top goalscorers in the Italian first</p>
<p>division after the final day of the serie A season on Sunday (a</p>
<p>total of 808 goals were scored):</p>
<p>24 - Filippo Inzaghi (Atalanta)</p>
<p>22 - Vincenzo Montella (Sampdoria)</p>
<p>17 - Abel Balbo (Roma)</p>
<p>16 - Sandro Tovalieri (12 with Cagliari, 4 with Reggiana)</p>
<p>15 - Roberto Mancini (Sampdoria), Marco Negri (Perugia),</p>
<p>Giuseppe Signori (Lazio)</p>
<p>14 - Enrico Chiesa (Parma), Youri Djorkaeff (Inter), Pasquale</p>
<p>Luiso (Piacenza)</p>
<p>13 - Marcelo Otero (Vicenza), George Weah (Milan), Paolo Poggi</p>
<p>and Oliver Bierhoff (both Udinese)</p>
<p>12 - Marcio Amoroso (Udinese), Gabriele Batistuta (Fiorentina),</p>
<p>Filippo Maniero (Verona), Hernan Crespo (Parma)</p>
<p>11 - Igor Kolyvanov (Bologna), Anselmo Robbiati (Fiorentina),</p>
<p>Maurizio Ganz (Inter)</p>
<p>10 - Roberto Muzzi (Cagliari)</p>
<p>9 - Alfredo Aglietti (Napoli), Luis Oliveira (Fiorentina)</p>
<p>8 - Demetrio Albertini (Milan), Kennet Andersson (Bologna),</p>
<p>Alessandro Del Piero, Michele Padovano and Christian Vieri all</p>
<p>Juventus), Pierluigi Casiraghi (Lazio)</p>
<p>7 - Paul Ince and Ivan Zamorano (Inter), Nicola Caccia</p>
<p>(Napoli), Pavel Nedved and Igor Protti (both Lazio)</p>
<p>6 - Gabriele Ambrosetti and Roberto Murgita (both Vicenza),</p>
<p>Marco Carparelli (Sampdoria), Antonio De Vitis and Pierluigi</p>
<p>Orlandini (both Verona), Vladimir Jugovic (Juventus),  Igor</p>
<p>Simutenkov (Reggiana)</p>
</text>
